    {
      "id": "92jxou9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "scwvrfv",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ohpx43",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ndhloxh",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "psvo7dt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lamx4ar",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1b8xp2e",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9o4d12g",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Litmus turns RED in acidic solution and BLUE in basic solution.",
        "Phenolphthalein indicator is COLORLESS in acids and PINK in bases.",
        "Strong acids (e.g., HCl, H2SO4) completely dissociate in water, while weak acids (e.g., CH3COOH) only partially dissociate.",
        "Neutralization reactions are exothermic and consistently produce salt plus water."
      ],
      "id": "jv0u78y"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ik9lfa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ks5j5w0",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oi23z8l",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u77m6wi",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "4n09sdt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q85kk2d",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rxorbbc",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "66pfejw",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pgdiczk",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}